cff-version: 1.2.0
title: LnFinder
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file. The
  author list of the accompanying publication is not recorded here yet (see the note
  at the top of this file), and neither is a DOI; both are added when the archived
  release is made.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Peeters
    given-names: Stijn
abstract: >-
  Julia tooling for finding PQQ-dependent alcohol dehydrogenases in large sequence
  sets and calling the metal cofactor of each one — lanthanide or calcium — from the
  residue found at the calibrated active-site column of a profile HMM. The package
  also carries the control-set validation of that call, the taxonomy and habitat
  tooling built around it, and a library for looking for further specificity
  determinants in the alignment and in structures.
# SPDX identifier of the licence that covers the software. One data file,
# dat/models/methanol_dehydrogenase_pqq_xoxF_mxaF.hmm, is third-party and is excluded
# from that grant; see the "Exceptions" section of LICENSE and dat/models/PROVENANCE.md.
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - lanthanide
  - calcium
  - methanol dehydrogenase
  - PQQ
  - profile hidden Markov model
  - sequence analysis
  - Julia
# The third-party databases and services this software reads are listed, with their
# endpoints, under "Data sources" in README.md. Citing this software does not cite them;
# cite them yourself if you use the data. The profile HMM shipped under dat/models/ carries
# its own citation and licence status in dat/models/PROVENANCE.md, and the third-party rows
# of the control set carry theirs in the header of dat/control_set/known_cofactor_mdhs.tsv.
# A `references:` block with each database's own publication and DOI is added at release,
# alongside the author list and the release DOI; no DOI is guessed here.
